`Outbox.due` now returns a fresh empty array when `isQuiet(this.quiet, now)` is true, using the file's existing `isQuiet` helper and the outbox's own quiet hours. Outside quiet hours the code is unchanged.

I couldn't see the body of `isQuiet`, so I'm assuming it takes a full stamp as its second argument (as its `at: number` signature suggests) and handles the overnight wrap (21:00 to 08:00) itself. `due` receives `now` as a stamp, so I passed it straight through.
